# Copy Turn and Export to Clipboard render an element row through ONE body
# arm: a heading naming the element (with its provenance in brackets when
# there is any), then the projection inside a text fence that is LONGER than
# any run of backticks inside the projection -- the CommonMark rule -- so a
# projection that itself holds ``` still closes. Copy Message on the row
# copies the projection alone, byte for byte, markdown characters included.
#
# The mock's HANABI_ELEMENTS_DEMO thread: a pinned table at rev 2, an inline
# note whose projection carries a ```-run (its fence must be four ticks), and
# an artifact-placed card with an empty projection (its body is its heading).
# ADDED, NOT RUN in the source lane.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":[],"active_tab":"","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_ELEMENTS_DEMO=1 HANABI_OPEN=relements

require_thread relements
expect_text_drawn "| C | ok | 0s |" within=60

# Export to Clipboard from the thread's row: the whole conversation as
# loaded, every row through body_of, no trailing trim -- exact bytes.
reset_clipboard_probe
right_click_ui chat_row_id_relements
wait_frames 8
expect_text "Export to Clipboard"
click_ui row_menu_export_clipboard
wait_frames 8
expect_clipboard_escaped "# shard health table\n\n### **You**\n\nshow me the shard health table\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nHere is the current shard health.\n\n### **Element: Shard health** (pinned · std/Table · rev 2)\n\n```text\n| shard | status | lag |\n| A | ok | 0s |\n| B | ok | 1s |\n| C | ok | 0s |\n```\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nShard C recovered; the table above is updated in place.\n\n### **Element: std/Note**\n\n````text\nQuote the query as ```sql ... ``` in the doc; **these ticks and stars are literal** and <b>so is this</b>.\n````\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nNothing else needs you.\n\n### **Element: Run summary** (artifact art_9 · std/Card)\n\n```text\nRun summary\n```\n\n"

# Copy Turn from the table's provenance line -- the menu is offered on the
# whole element block, head, provenance and body alike: the same rows, the
# same bytes per row, trimmed of the trailing blank line as every Copy Turn
# is.
reset_clipboard_probe
right_click_text "rev 2"
wait_frames 6
expect_text "Copy Turn"
click_text "Copy Turn"
wait_frames 6
expect_clipboard_escaped "### **You**\n\nshow me the shard health table\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nHere is the current shard health.\n\n### **Element: Shard health** (pinned · std/Table · rev 2)\n\n```text\n| shard | status | lag |\n| A | ok | 0s |\n| B | ok | 1s |\n| C | ok | 0s |\n```\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nShard C recovered; the table above is updated in place.\n\n### **Element: std/Note**\n\n````text\nQuote the query as ```sql ... ``` in the doc; **these ticks and stars are literal** and <b>so is this</b>.\n````\n\n### **Agentcloud**\n\nNothing else needs you.\n\n### **Element: Run summary** (artifact art_9 · std/Card)\n\n```text\nRun summary\n```\n"

# Copy Message on the note copies its projection alone: the ticks, the
# stars and the tag are bytes, not formatting, and nothing is added.
reset_clipboard_probe
right_click_text "std/Note"
wait_frames 6
expect_text "Copy Message"
click_text "Copy Message"
wait_frames 6
expect_clipboard "Quote the query as ```sql ... ``` in the doc; **these ticks and stars are literal** and <b>so is this</b>."

# Copy Message from a body line of the table copies the whole rev-2
# projection, not rev 1 and not the one line.
reset_clipboard_probe
right_click_text "| A | ok | 0s |"
wait_frames 6
click_text "Copy Message"
wait_frames 6
expect_clipboard_escaped "| shard | status | lag |\n| A | ok | 0s |\n| B | ok | 1s |\n| C | ok | 0s |"
